IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division D, "Return to be filed": sections 30, 31, 32 and 35. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- A person who must contribute on self-employed earnings files a return of those earnings with the Minister by the day the
-- income tax return is due (section 30), estimates the contributions in it (section 31), and is assessed (section 32). A
-- late return attracts a penalty (section 35). If no return is filed and the Minister does not assess within four years,
-- the contribution is deemed to be zero (subsection 30(5)).
--
-- The day the income tax return is due, the contribution the person is required to make, and the Income Tax Act penalty
-- are facts of other provisions or of an Act that is not deposited: each is a plain input with a comment "out of range".
-- Every rule is constitutive (BOOLEAN, NUMBER, DATE or an enumeration).

§ `Division D -- Collection of Contributions in Respect of Self-Employed Earnings`

§§ `s 30 -- the return of self-employed earnings`

-- src:779 | Return to be filed
-- src:780 | 30 (1) Where a person is required to make a contribution for a year in respect of self-employed earnings, a return of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year shall, without notice or demand for it, be filed with the Minister in the prescribed form and manner and containing the prescribed information, by that person (or, if the person is unable for any reason to file the return, by their representative) on or before the day on or before which the person’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required by that Part to be filed or would be required by that Part to be filed if tax under that Part were payable for the year.
@ref Act s 30(1) (src:779-780)
GIVEN `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 10 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) — a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year must be filed without notice or demand` `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MEANS
    `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings`

@ref Act s 30(1) (src:779-780)
DECLARE `cp2 Who must file the return of self-employed earnings` IS ONE OF
    `the person must file the return`
    `the person's representative must file the return`
    `the text does not say who must file the return`
    `no return is required under subsection 30(1)`

-- "by that person (or, if the person is unable for any reason to file the return, by their representative)".
-- A person unable to file who has no representative is not decided by the text.
@ref Act s 30(1) (src:779-780)
GIVEN `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is unable for any reason to file the return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of representative the person has` IS A `Kind of representative`
GIVETH A `cp2 Who must file the return of self-employed earnings`
`s 30(1) — who must file the return` `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the person is unable for any reason to file the return` `the kind of representative the person has` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 30(1) — a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year must be filed without notice or demand` `the person is required to make a contribution for the year in respect of self-employed earnings`) THEN `no return is required under subsection 30(1)`
        IF (NOT `the person is unable for any reason to file the return`) THEN `the person must file the return`
        IF `s 2(1) — a representative of a person` `the kind of representative the person has` THEN `the person's representative must file the return`
        OTHERWISE `the text does not say who must file the return`

-- "on or before the day on or before which the person's return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act is required by that Part to be
-- filed or would be required by that Part to be filed if tax under that Part were payable for the year".
@ref Act s 30(1) (src:779-780)
GIVEN `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year` IS A DATE -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
GIVETH A DATE
`s 30(1) — the last day for filing the return of self-employed earnings` `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year` MEANS
    `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year`

@ref Act s 30(1) (src:779-780)
GIVEN `the day the return is filed` IS A DATE
      `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) — the return is filed in time` `the day the return is filed` `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year` MEANS
    `the day the return is filed` AT MOST (`s 30(1) — the last day for filing the return of self-employed earnings` `the day the person's income tax return is due under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or would be due if tax were payable for the year`)

-- src:781 | Demand for return
-- src:782 | (2) Whether or not he is liable to make a contribution for a year in respect of his self-employed earnings and whether or not a return has been filed under subsection (1), every person shall, on demand from the Minister, served personally or by registered letter, file with the Minister in prescribed form and containing prescribed information, within such reasonable time as may be stipulated in the demand, a return of his self-employed earnings for the year designated therein.
@ref Act s 30(2) (src:781-782)
GIVEN `the Minister demanded the return from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand was served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand was served by registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) — the person must file a return of self-employed earnings for the year designated in the demand` `the Minister demanded the return from the person` `the demand was served personally` `the demand was served by registered letter` MEANS
        `the Minister demanded the return from the person`
    AND (`the demand was served personally` OR `the demand was served by registered letter`)

-- The time is "such reasonable time as may be stipulated in the demand": the last day is the one the demand names, and
-- whether the stipulated time is reasonable is for the Minister's demand to satisfy (a judgment the text hands to the Minister).
@ref Act s 30(2) (src:781-782)
GIVEN `the day the return is filed` IS A DATE
      `the last day the demand stipulates for filing the return` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) — the return is filed within the time the demand stipulates` `the day the return is filed` `the last day the demand stipulates for filing the return` MEANS
    `the day the return is filed` AT MOST `the last day the demand stipulates for filing the return`

-- src:783 | Return by trustee, etc.
-- src:784 | (3) Every trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee and every agent or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or income of a person who has not filed a return of his self-employed earnings for a year as required by this section shall file with the Minister a return in prescribed form of that person’s self-employed earnings for the year.
@ref Act s 30(3) (src:783-784)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee, or an agent or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or income of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person has not filed a return of self-employed earnings for the year as required by section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) — the person must file a return of the other person's self-employed earnings for the year` `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee, or an agent or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or income of another person` `the other person has not filed a return of self-employed earnings for the year as required by section 30` MEANS
        `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee, or an agent or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business, estate or income of another person`
    AND `the other person has not filed a return of self-employed earnings for the year as required by section 30`

-- The province is identified "on the last day of that year": the keel's year rule gives that day. (Subsection 4(5), which
-- is the keel's, fixes a different day for paragraph 4(1)(b) when the person left Canada during the year; subsection 30(4)
-- says "the last day of that year" and is read literally: fork F18.)
-- src:785 | Identification of province of residence
-- src:786 | (4) The prescribed information to be contained in any return of the self-employed earnings of a person for a year required by this section to be filed with the Minister shall identify the province in which that person was resident on the last day of that year.
@ref Act s 30(4) (src:785-786)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 30(4) — the day as at which the return must identify the person's province of residence` year MEANS
    `s 2(1) — the last day of a year` year

@ref Act s 30(4) (src:785-786)
GIVEN `the province named in the return` IS A STRING
      `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(4) — the return identifies the province as required` `the province named in the return` `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year` MEANS
    `the province named in the return` EQUALS `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year`

-- src:787 | Where no return filed within four years
-- src:788 | (5) The amount of any contribution required by this Act to be made by a person for a year in respect of their self-employed earnings for the year is deemed to be zero where
-- src:789 | (a) the return of those earnings required by this section to be filed with the Minister is not filed with the Minister before the day that is four years after the day on or before which the return is required by subsection (1) to be filed; and
-- src:790 | (b) the Minister does not assess the contribution before the end of those four years.
@ref Act s 30(5) (src:787-790)
GIVEN `the day on or before which the return is required by subsection 30(1) to be filed` IS A DATE
      `the day the return was filed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Minister assessed the contribution, if the Minister has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(5) — the contribution for the year is deemed to be zero` `the day on or before which the return is required by subsection 30(1) to be filed` `the day the return was filed, if it has been` `the day the Minister assessed the contribution, if the Minister has` MEANS
        `the return was not filed before the day four years after the due day`
    AND `the Minister did not assess the contribution before the end of those four years`
    WHERE
        `the day four years after the due day` MEANS
            `the date a time limit ends` `the day on or before which the return is required by subsection 30(1) to be filed` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 4)
        -- (a): "is not filed ... before the day that is four years after": filing on that day itself is not "before" it.
        `the return was not filed before the day four years after the due day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the return was filed, if it has been`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST filed THEN filed AT LEAST `the day four years after the due day`
        -- (b): the four years end on that day, so an assessment on it is still "before the end" (fork F19).
        `the Minister did not assess the contribution before the end of those four years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the Minister assessed the contribution, if the Minister has`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST assessed THEN assessed GREATER THAN `the day four years after the due day`

@ref Act s 30(5) (src:787-790)
GIVEN `the contribution otherwise required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contribution is deemed to be zero under subsection 30(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(5) — the contribution required for the year after subsection 30(5)` `the contribution otherwise required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contribution is deemed to be zero under subsection 30(5)` MEANS
    IF `the contribution is deemed to be zero under subsection 30(5)`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the contribution otherwise required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings`

§§ `s 31 and 32 -- the estimate, and the assessment`

-- src:791 | Estimate to be made
-- src:792 | 31 Every person who is required by section 30 to file a return of the person’s self-employed earnings shall in the return estimate the amount of the contributions to be made by the person in respect of those earnings.
@ref Act s 31 (src:791-792)
GIVEN `the person is required by section 30 to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31 — the person must estimate in the return the contributions to be made on the self-employed earnings` `the person is required by section 30 to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings` MEANS
    `the person is required by section 30 to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings`

-- src:793 | Examination of return and notice of assessment
-- src:794 | 32 The Minister shall, with all due dispatch, examine each return of self-employed earnings and assess the contributions for the year in respect of those earnings and the interest and penalties, if any, payable, and, after the examination, shall send a notice of assessment to the person by whom the return was filed.
@ref Act s 32 (src:793-794)
GIVEN `a return of self-employed earnings has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32 — the Minister must examine the return, assess the contributions, interest and penalties, and send a notice of assessment to the person who filed the return` `a return of self-employed earnings has been filed` MEANS
    `a return of self-employed earnings has been filed`

@ref Act s 32 (src:793-794)
GIVEN `the contributions for the year in respect of the self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest payable, if any` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalties payable, if any` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 32 — the total the assessment states` `the contributions for the year in respect of the self-employed earnings` `the interest payable, if any` `the penalties payable, if any` MEANS
    `the contributions for the year in respect of the self-employed earnings` PLUS `the interest payable, if any` PLUS `the penalties payable, if any`

§§ `s 35 -- penalties for not filing`

-- (1): 5% of the part of the contributions that remained unpaid when the time for filing the return expired. The Minister may
-- reduce or remit the penalty if the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act
-- (a judgment handed to the Minister, so the reduction is a conditional input, never guessed).
-- src:829 | Failure to file a return
-- src:830 | 35 (1) Every person who fails to file a return of the person’s self-employed earnings for a year as and when required by section 30 is liable to a penalty of 5% of the part of the amount of the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the contributions that remained unpaid at the expiration of the time the return was required to be filed, except that, if that person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year, the Minister may reduce the penalty to which the person is liable under this section or may remit the penalty in whole or in part.
@ref Act s 35(1) (src:829-830)
GIVEN `the person failed to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year as and when required by section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the contributions for the year that remained unpaid at the expiration of the time the return was required to be filed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 35(1) — the penalty for failing to file the return` `the person failed to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year as and when required by section 30` `the part of the contributions for the year that remained unpaid at the expiration of the time the return was required to be filed` MEANS
    IF `the person failed to file a return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year as and when required by section 30`
    THEN `the part of the contributions for the year that remained unpaid at the expiration of the time the return was required to be filed` TIMES 5%
    ELSE 0

@ref Act s 35(1) (src:829-830)
GIVEN penalty IS A NUMBER
      `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
      `the amount by which the Minister reduces or remits the penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 35(1) — the penalty after any reduction or remission by the Minister` penalty `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year` `the amount by which the Minister reduces or remits the penalty` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection 162(1) or (2) of the Income Tax Act in respect of the year`
    THEN max 0 (penalty MINUS `the amount by which the Minister reduces or remits the penalty`)
    ELSE penalty

-- src:831 | Idem
-- src:832 | (2) Every person who fails to file a return as required by subsection 30(3) is liable to a penalty of five dollars for each day of default, but not exceeding in all fifty dollars.
@ref Act s 35(2) (src:831-832)
GIVEN `the person failed to file a return as required by subsection 30(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 35(2) — the penalty for failing to file the return required by subsection 30(3)` `the person failed to file a return as required by subsection 30(3)` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    IF `the person failed to file a return as required by subsection 30(3)`
    THEN min 50 (5 TIMES `the number of days of default`)
    ELSE 0
